From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:05:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): render chat link rules and edit them in Settings

Short references in chat messages (BST-2135, PR #123, session:<id>) are plain
text today. This renders the user's link rules from /v1/link-rules and adds a
Settings group to edit them.

- web/src/lib/linkRules.ts checks and compiles a rule with the same checks as
  the server, so a rule that slipped past it still can't run, and links text
  through a remark pass after item labels have become chips. Like item
  labels, it never rewrites links (file links included), inline code, code
  blocks or raw HTML, and it applies to agent and user messages. Compiled
  regexes take their leading boundary as a group instead of lookbehind, which
  older Safari can't parse. Captures are percent-encoded and every href is
  re-parsed as http(s) before use.
- Git references follow the session's repository, read from the git info
  the PR panel already fetches: the git rule for its host (or, unlisted, the
  provider the server resolved) links #123, issue #123, PR #123 / MR #123 and
  the provider's !123 with GitHub, GitLab or Azure DevOps URL shapes. Without
  a repository a bare #123 stays text. The GitHub rule links owner/repo#123
  in every session; in a session on another host, a qualified reference under
  the session's top-level group, with more than two segments or with !, stays
  on that host. The runner's GitHub, GitLab and Azure DevOps resources report
  the repository URL, so a session with no PR knows its host.
- session:<id>[/<message id>] opens /c/<id>?message=<message id> in the app,
  the deep link item labels use for Show in conversation.
- Streamdown's memo ignores remarkPlugins, so a message is keyed on its
  matchers and re-parses once when the rules or repository arrive; the
  repository keeps its identity across PR panel polls.
- Settings > General > Chat links lists, adds (url rules and git hosts),
  edits, toggles, deletes and resets rules, shows each rule's error, and
  previews sample text with the rules being edited.

Not upstream yet: proposed from feat/chat-link-rules, the git-reference part from
feat/git-ref-notation; drop this copy once they merge.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
